# Prospective V4 inherited-claim owner and resolver encoding

Actual author: `/root`, 2026-10-10 UTC. This new addendum applies only to a future `belief-gap-v4` candidate after these bytes are frozen. Read it with the unchanged V1/V2/V3 public definitions and `BELIEF_CONTROL_PROPERTIES_METADATA_V4.md` (SHA256 `40b552ecf47c11bfffb2669283640dda991d6dc6e7094ed3051fb9cad2489fce`). It changes no visible task, target, semantic property, world table, split or source family. It approves no data and applies no retrospective rule to V3.

The V4 clarification explicitly matches coordinates between the two evidence records, but describes the claim-bearing row's matching-length selection as the simplest encoding. For this future V4 candidate, the following owner and resolution requirements are mandatory for each supplied `corpus_variant` claim of either `same_prefix_empty_nonempty_counterfactual` or `contradiction_equals_mixed_outcomes`.

1. Resolve the claim's two actual `pair_sample_ids` from the supplied candidate. Both evidence records must match the claim-bearing row's `source_family_key`, `auxiliary_scalar_variant`, `schedule_index` and `renderer`. Compare declared metadata and actual decoded inputs; a sample-ID spelling or annotation alone is insufficient. The claim-bearing row may be any A–H context and need not be a member of its evidence pair. This remains a family relationship, with no implied per-row empty/nonempty status.
2. Use the actual number of observations in the claim-bearing row's visible task. At length 2, the pair is its matched E/G records, ordered empty E first and nonempty G second. At length 3, it is its matched F/H records, ordered empty F first and nonempty H second. Both evidence members have that same length. Every previously published typed-world, query, observation-difference, first-prefix and opposite-outcome requirement remains independently recomputed. Neither length can stand in for the other in complete cohort coverage.
3. Resolve `evidence_manifest` to the actual supplied manifest file. Within its published `supplied_same_table_v2_pairs` collection, lookup by the exact `control_id`, inherited identifier and ordered `pair_sample_ids` must yield exactly one named entry. That entry carries the V4 published minimum fields and the exact complete candidate SHA256. Its family, scalar variant and observation length must match the resolved records. Duplicate entries with the same lookup key are invalid. Reuse of one descriptive control ID for the two different inherited identifiers on the same truthful pair is permitted; no global uniqueness, private prefix or particular ID syntax is required.

The original canonical claim field vocabulary stays closed. This addendum adds no canonical field and imposes no closed top-level manifest schema. Additional manifest diagnostics may be preserved, but cannot replace the required resolved entry or independently derived relationship. An explicit `pair_record_hashes` field is not required: validate the actual resolved records' full hashes and the manifest's exact complete candidate hash. Extra hashes are optional custody evidence, with no authority to override actual inputs.

The three V3 aggregate controls retain their existing public encoding and complete-group requirements. Executed `audit_probe` records remain separately attributed and cannot substitute for either inherited supplied pair. This addendum introduces no extra probe requirement, row property, witness name, semantic task or family.

Before any V4 producer source or candidate is generated, freeze a new independently authored checker and positive/negative tests against all these public bytes. Include a legitimate nonmember owner, both lengths and scalar variants, shared IDs across the two names, and rejection of wrong owner coordinates, reversed/foreign pairs, duplicate lookup keys, missing/mismatched named entries, incorrect candidate hashes and unexecuted probe substitutions. Test from handmade public inputs. Preserve prior specifications, checkers, failures, candidates and first judgments unchanged. The actual later V4 source and complete cohort still require exact-byte reproduction, separate fresh reviews and independent adjudication.

The intended revision reuses the existing 3,456 visible input/target triples and four source families only if exact row-by-row comparison proves preservation. Added semantic-task and family counts are zero. Prior canonical exposure, correlated views, finite-corpus shortcuts, exposed development splits, common-model execution and design/adjudicator overlap remain disclosed. No learning, model, architecture, sealed-evaluation or efficacy claim follows from this metadata clarification.
